=-7 \\cdot ∇_{w}(w^{T}x) + 3 \\cdot ∇_{w}(w^{T}w) - ∇_{w}(2) \\\\\n&=-7 \\cdot x + 3 \\cdot 2w - 0 \\\\\n&=-7x + 6w\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535844 17592186045417 false] [17592186203864 1074 "Using the results \n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf w}(\\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}, \\qquad \\nabla_{\\mathbf w} (\\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{w}) = 2\\mathbf{w},\n$$\n\n \nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}(-7{w}^{T}x+3‖w{‖}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)+3\\cdot {∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}^{2})-{∇}_{w}(2) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)+3\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}w)-{∇}_{w}(2) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot x+3\\cdot 2w-0 \\\\  & =-7x+6w.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535844 17592186045417 true] [17592186203874 1071 "Given the function\n$f(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{w}) = \\left.-3\\left(\\|\\mathbf{w}\\\\right|_1\\right)^3 - 5\\mathbf x^T\\mathbf w$\nthat maps a vector to a scalar, find $\\nabla_{\\mathbf w}f$. You may assume that $\\mathbf w$ has no zero components." 13194139535844 17592186045417 false] [17592186203874 1071 "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{w}) = -3\\left(\\|\\mathbf{w}\\|_1\\right)^3  - 5\\mathbf x^T\\mathbf w\n$$\n\nthat maps a vector to a scalar, find $\\nabla_{\\mathbf w}f.$ You may assume that $\\mathbf w$ has no zero components." 13194139535844 17592186045417 true] [17592186203874 1074 "Using the results\n\n$$\n\\left.\\nabla_{\\mathbf w} (\\|\\mathbf{w}\\\\right|_1) = \\text{sign}(\\mathbf{w}), \\qquad \\nabla_{\\mathbf w}\\left(\\mathbf x^T\\mathbf w\\right) = \\mathbf x\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇_{w}f &= ∇_{w}(-3(‖w‖_{1})^{3} - 5x^{T}w) \\\\\n&= ∇_{w}(-3(‖w‖_{1})^{3}) - ∇_{w}(5x^{T}w) \\\\\n&=-3 \\cdot ∇_{w}((‖w‖_{1})^{3}) - 5 \\cdot ∇_{w}(x^{T}w) \\\\\n&=-3 \\cdot 3(‖w‖_{1})^{2} \\cdot ∇_{w}(‖w‖_{1}) - 5 \\cdot x \\\\\n&=-3 \\cdot 3(‖w‖_{1})^{2} \\cdot sign(w) - 5 \\cdot x \\\\\n&=-9(‖w‖_{1})^{2} \\cdot sign(w) - 5x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535844 17592186045417 false] [17592186203874 1074 "Using the results\n\n$$\n\